---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | 282 Munro Bagging App"
  description="Privacy policy for the 282 Munro bagging app for iOS and Android."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
    <article class="prose prose-gray mt-6">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        Alastair McNeill built the 282 app as a Free app. This SERVICE is provided by Alastair
        McNeill at no cost and is intended for use as is.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page is used to inform visitors regarding my policies with the collection, use, and
        disclosure of Personal Information if anyone decided to use my Service.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose to use my Service, then you agree to the collection and use of information in
        relation to this policy. The Personal Information that I collect is used for providing and
        improving the Service. I will not use or share your information with anyone except as
        described in this Privacy Policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        The terms used in this Privacy Policy have the same meanings as in our
        <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> unless otherwise defined in this Privacy Policy.
      </p>
      <h2>Information Collection and Use</h2>
      <p>
        For a better experience, while using our Service, I may require you to provide us with
        certain personally identifiable information, including but not limited to email, name. The
        information that I request will be retained on your device and is not collected by me in
        any way.
      </p>
      <p>The app does use third-party services that may collect information used to identify you.</p>
      <p>Link to the privacy policy of third-party service providers used by the app:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Play Services</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.strava.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Strava</a> (only if you connect it)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Strava</h2>
      <p>
        You can choose to connect your Strava account so that 282 can find the Munros you've
        climbed. This is optional, and nothing is read from Strava until you connect.
      </p>
      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <p>
        With your permission (the <code>activity:read</code> scope), 282 reads your Strava athlete
        ID and your activities: name, sport type, date and start time, elapsed time, distance,
        elevation and the recording device. It also reads each activity's route, but only uses it
        to check which Munros it passed. The route and start/end locations are never stored.
        Activities you've set to "Only You" on Strava are not visible to 282. Your Strava access
        tokens are stored encrypted.
      </p>
      <h3>How we collect it</h3>
      <p>
        Strava notifies 282 when you upload, change or delete an activity, and 282 then reads that
        one activity. If you ask 282 to scan your history, it reads your activity list once; the
        results are shown to you and are not stored.
      </p>
      <h3>How we use it and who can see it</h3>
      <p>
        Strava data is used only to suggest Munros for you to confirm. It is shown only to you. It
        is never shared with other 282 users, sold, used for advertising, used for analytics, or
        used to train or run any artificial intelligence. If you choose to share a post that was
        filled in from a Strava activity, 282 asks you first, and only the details you choose to
        post are shared.
      </p>
      <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
      <p>
        282 only keeps activities that passed a Munro, and only until you review them or for 7
        days, whichever comes first. They are then deleted automatically. Munros you confirm become
        part of your 282 log, like any Munro you log by hand.
      </p>
      <h3>Seeing your data, withdrawing consent and deletion</h3>
      <p>
        You can see everything 282 currently holds from Strava in Settings → Your Strava data. You
        can withdraw consent at any time by tapping Disconnect from Strava in Settings, or by
        revoking 282 in your
        <a href="https://www.strava.com/settings/apps" rel="noopener">Strava settings</a>. Either
        way, 282 permanently deletes all data it obtained from Strava for you, usually immediately
        and always within 30 days, and confirms in the app when deletion is complete. You can also
        email the address below to ask for a copy of your data or for it to be deleted.
      </p>
      <h3>Strava's role</h3>
      <p>
        Strava may collect and use data about 282's use of the Strava API ("Usage Data") for any
        business purpose, including improving the Strava API, providing support and checking
        compliance with its API Agreement. Strava's handling of your data is governed by the
        <a href="https://www.strava.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Strava Privacy Policy</a>,
        which takes precedence over this policy where they conflict.
      </p>
      <h3>Where it's processed</h3>
      <p>
        Strava data is stored and processed by Supabase (database and server functions) on 282's
        behalf. Sign-in is handled by Google Firebase.
      </p>
      <h2>Log Data</h2>
      <p>
        I want to inform you that whenever you use my Service, in a case of an error in the app I
        collect data and information (through third-party products) on your phone called Log Data.
        This Log Data may include information such as your device Internet Protocol ("IP") address,
        device name, operating system version, the configuration of the app when utilizing my
        Service, the time and date of your use of the Service, and other statistics.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are files with a small amount of data that are commonly used as anonymous unique
        identifiers. These are sent to your browser from the websites that you visit and are stored
        on your device's internal memory.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Service does not use these "cookies" explicitly. However, the app may use third-party
        code and libraries that use "cookies" to collect information and improve their services.
        You have the option to either accept or refuse these cookies and know when a cookie is
        being sent to your device. If you choose to refuse our cookies, you may not be able to use
        some portions of this Service.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website (282app.uk) uses an optional analytics cookie (Google Analytics) only if you
        accept it via the cookie banner. You can browse the whole site without accepting.
      </p>
      <h2>Service Providers</h2>
      <p>I may employ third-party companies and individuals due to the following reasons:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To facilitate our Service;</li>
        <li>To provide the Service on our behalf;</li>
        <li>To perform Service-related services; or</li>
        <li>To assist us in analyzing how our Service is used.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I want to inform users of this Service that these third parties have access to their
        Personal Information. The reason is to perform the tasks assigned to them on our behalf.
        However, they are obligated not to disclose or use the information for any other purpose.
      </p>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        I value your trust in providing us your Personal Information, thus we are striving to use
        commercially acceptable means of protecting it. But remember that no method of transmission
        over the internet, or method of electronic storage is 100% secure and reliable, and I
        cannot guarantee its absolute security.
      </p>
      <h2>Links to Other Sites</h2>
      <p>
        This Service may contain links to other sites. If you click on a third-party link, you will
        be directed to that site. Note that these external sites are not operated by me. Therefore,
        I strongly advise you to review the Privacy Policy of these websites. I have no control
        over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any
        third-party sites or services.
      </p>
      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        These Services do not address anyone under the age of 13. I do not knowingly collect
        personally identifiable information from children under 13 years of age. In the case I
        discover that a child under 13 has provided me with personal information, I immediately
        delete this from our servers. If you are a parent or guardian and you are aware that your
        child has provided us with personal information, please contact me so that I will be able
        to do the necessary actions.
      </p>
      <h2>Deleting Your Account</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your 282 account and all associated data at any time from within the app.
        See <a href="/delete-account">how to delete your account</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        I may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Thus, you are advised to review this
        page periodically for any changes. I will notify you of any changes by posting the new
        Privacy Policy on this page.
      </p>
      <p>This policy is effective as of 2023-10-18.</p>
      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions or suggestions about my Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to
        contact me at
        <a href="mailto:alastair.r.mcneill@gmail.com">alastair.r.mcneill@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
